<title>USA: US Airlines ahead of ordered move to quieter jets.</title>
<headline>US Airlines ahead of ordered move to quieter jets.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. airlines are ahead of a federal deadline to retire all their older, noiser jets in favor of new quieter ones by the year 2000, Transportation Secretary Federico Pena said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>He said that in the past year, more than 200 of the noisiest so-called stage 2 planes have been taken out of service in favor of such quieter stage 3 planes as the Boeing Co 777 and the McDonnell Douglas Corp MD-80.</p>
</text>
